1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:03,945
Knowledge graph embedding models can rank
candidate links,

2
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:06,597
but a ranking alone does not tell a
curator

3
00:00:06,668 --> 00:00:08,668
whether a prediction should be accepted,

4
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:13,120
verified, escalated, rejected, or left
unresolved.

5
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:17,933
KGEC-Agent addresses this gap by
converting

6
00:00:18,254 --> 00:00:21,816
calibrated confidence into an explicit
curation action.

7
00:00:22,536 --> 00:00:25,074
A language model interprets the request

8
00:00:25,495 --> 00:00:28,120
and coordinates eight specialized tools.

9
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:32,295
The KGE component proposes candidates,

10
00:00:32,632 --> 00:00:35,994
KGEC provides calibrated probabilities,

11
00:00:36,294 --> 00:00:39,319
and a confidence policy selects the
initial route.

12
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:42,629
Evidence retrieval and semantic validation

13
00:00:42,811 --> 00:00:44,949
then determine the final decision,

14
00:00:45,273 --> 00:00:48,448
while provenance records how that decision
was reached.

15
00:00:48,959 --> 00:00:51,996
The language model cannot alter confidence
values,

16
00:00:52,296 --> 00:00:54,921
policy thresholds, evidence results,

17
00:00:55,258 --> 00:00:58,145
semantic constraints, or candidate
admission.

18
00:00:59,264 --> 00:01:02,689
This recording uses reviewed deterministic
fixtures

19
00:01:02,716 --> 00:01:05,769
so that the complete agent workflow can be
replayed

20
00:01:05,779 --> 00:01:07,794
without external services.

21
00:01:07,923 --> 00:01:10,923
The three workflows demonstrate system
behaviour

22
00:01:10,938 --> 00:01:13,188
rather than benchmark performance.

23
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:16,720
In the automatic-acceptance workflow,

24
00:01:16,904 --> 00:01:19,329
the natural-language request is mapped

25
00:01:19,362 --> 00:01:21,987
to a structured link-prediction query.

26
00:01:22,299 --> 00:01:25,262
The system produces a ranked candidate
list

27
00:01:25,395 --> 00:01:29,120
together with raw scores and calibrated
probabilities.

28
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:33,170
The Top-1 confidence is 0.92

29
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:37,186
and the Top-1 versus Top-2 margin is 0.86.

30
00:01:37,285 --> 00:01:39,998
Both satisfy the acceptance policy.

31
00:01:40,072 --> 00:01:42,472
All seven semantic checks pass,

32
00:01:42,482 --> 00:01:45,010
so the final decision is accepted

33
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,517
and the prediction is staged

34
00:01:46,527 --> 00:01:49,142
in the separate accepted-candidate graph.

35
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:55,033
In the second workflow, the Top-1
confidence is 0.72.

36
00:01:55,248 --> 00:01:58,348
The confidence policy selects verification

37
00:01:58,367 --> 00:02:00,755
rather than immediate acceptance.

38
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:04,433
The agent invokes the configured local
evidence source,

39
00:02:04,443 --> 00:02:07,140
but no supporting evidence is found.

40
00:02:08,145 --> 00:02:10,645
The semantic checks still pass.

41
00:02:10,695 --> 00:02:14,395
Because the evidence requirement remains
unresolved,

42
00:02:14,405 --> 00:02:17,490
the candidate is sent to the human-review
queue

43
00:02:17,515 --> 00:02:20,390
instead of being staged automatically.

44
00:02:21,295 --> 00:02:24,245
The third workflow shows why confidence
alone

45
00:02:24,302 --> 00:02:25,852
is not sufficient.

46
00:02:26,175 --> 00:02:30,825
The candidate has a calibrated confidence
of 0.91

47
00:02:30,982 --> 00:02:34,120
and initially satisfies the acceptance
policy.

48
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:36,139
However,

49
00:02:36,163 --> 00:02:40,200
semantic validation detects a blocking
domain violation.

50
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:43,292
That violation overrides the initial
route,

51
00:02:43,302 --> 00:02:45,953
and the final decision becomes rejected.

52
00:02:46,007 --> 00:02:48,897
This separation ensures that high
confidence

53
00:02:48,907 --> 00:02:52,248
cannot bypass explicit knowledge-graph
constraints.

54
00:02:53,295 --> 00:02:57,245
Every run records the ordered execution of
all eight tools:

55
00:02:57,745 --> 00:03:00,995
prediction, calibration, confidence
routing,

56
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:04,020
evidence retrieval, semantic checking,

57
00:03:04,445 --> 00:03:07,095
final decision, candidate-graph routing,

58
00:03:07,470 --> 00:03:09,120
and provenance export.

59
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:13,870
The interface exposes reason codes,
evidence states,

60
00:03:14,139 --> 00:03:16,251
semantic outcomes, destinations,

61
00:03:16,445 --> 00:03:18,608
and input and output hashes.

62
00:03:19,014 --> 00:03:23,164
The complete record can be exported as
JSON, CSV,

63
00:03:23,445 --> 00:03:27,120
RDF Turtle using PROV-O, or Markdown.

64
00:03:28,245 --> 00:03:31,595
KGEC-Agent extends knowledge graph
completion

65
00:03:31,771 --> 00:03:33,796
from ranking candidate entities

66
00:03:34,071 --> 00:03:36,209
to deciding how each prediction should
enter

67
00:03:36,384 --> 00:03:39,947
an evidence-aware and auditable curation
process.

68
00:03:40,435 --> 00:03:43,785
The public repository provides the
complete offline replay,

69
00:03:44,077 --> 00:03:46,177
tests, sample exports,

70
00:03:46,469 --> 00:03:48,219
and reproducibility instructions

71
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,145
for all three workflows.
